    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d792">

                <pb facs="0842" n="828" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg828"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">621.2231/11–1344: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-13T19:00:00-05:00">November 13,
                            1944—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1889. Reference despatch number 4683, November 2, 1944. Foreign Office inquired
                    this morning whether Embassy could obtain early telegraphic reply to question
                    raised by Foreign Office in its memorandum of October 31<anchor n="73"
                        xml:id="d792-f1"/> regarding waiving of most-favored-nation rights in
                    connection with reciprocal extension of commercial advantages between Colombia
                    and neighboring nations. Matter apparently <pb facs="0843" n="829"
                        xml:id="pg829"/> considered urgent by Minister of Foreign Affairs because of
                    recent presentation to Colombian Congress of Colombian-Ecuadoran Treaty
                    (reference despatch number 4220 of August 12, 1944<anchor n="74"
                        xml:id="d792-f2"/>) for ratification. Full text of treaty<anchor n="75"
                        xml:id="d792-f3"/> as presented to Congress similar to text previously
                    reported and is being forwarded by air.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
